@@ -242,6 +244,24 @@
   It is possible to get statistics from the cFE ES application on the memory pool
   used by this application. #CFE_ES_SEND_MEM_POOL_STATS_CC is
   used to get statistics will need this memory pool handle as a command parameter.
+
+  <H2>10. Monitoring input staleness</H2>
+
+  For every copy table entry HK counts the consecutive combined sends of the
+  entry's output packet during which the entry's input data was not present
+  (the 'missed cycles').  The count is reset when a packet for the entry's input
+  MID arrives.  An entry is stale when its missed cycles reach the threshold
+  #HK_HkTlm_Payload_t.StaleCycles, which starts at #HK_STALE_CYCLES and can be
+  changed with #HK_SET_STALE_CYCLES_CC (1 to 255).  A new threshold is applied
+  at the next combined send of each output packet.
+
+  When an entry becomes stale HK sends #HK_INPUT_STALE_EID once and increments
+  #HK_HkTlm_Payload_t.StaleTransitionCtr; when its input arrives again (or a
+  raised threshold puts it below the limit) HK sends #HK_INPUT_FRESH_EID.
+  #HK_HkTlm_Payload_t.StaleInputCount shows how many entries are stale now, and
+  #HK_REPORT_STALE_CC sends an #HK_STALE_RPT_TLM_MID packet listing them.
+  #HK_RESET_COUNTERS_CC zeroes only the transition counter; loading a new copy
+  table clears all staleness history without events.
 **/
 
 /**
