+# HK input staleness tracking: implementation report
+
+## What changed
+
+### Flight software (`apps/hk`)
+
+| Area | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| `fsw/inc/hk_internal_cfg.h` | `HK_STALE_CYCLES` via `HK_INTERNAL_CFGVAL(STALE_CYCLES)`, `DEFAULT_HK_INTERNAL_STALE_CYCLES` = 3; range check 1..255 in `fsw/src/hk_verify.h` |
+| `config/default_hk_fcncode_values.h`, `fsw/inc/hk_fcncodes.h` | `HK_FunctionCode_SET_STALE_CYCLES = 2` / `HK_SET_STALE_CYCLES_CC`, `HK_FunctionCode_REPORT_STALE = 3` / `HK_REPORT_STALE_CC`, with command documentation |
+| `config/default_hk_msgdefs.h` | `HK_STALE_REPORT_MAX_ENTRIES` (16), `HK_SetStaleCycles_Payload_t`, `HK_StaleReport_Payload_t`; `HK_HkTlm_Payload_t` gets `StaleInputCount`, `StaleTransitionCtr`, `StaleCycles` and `Spare2[3]` after `MemPoolHandle` |
+| `config/default_hk_msgstruct.h` | `HK_SetStaleCyclesCmd_t`, `HK_ReportStaleCmd_t`, `HK_StaleReportTlm_t` |
+| `fsw/inc/hk_topicids.h`, `config/default_hk_msgids.h` | `CFE_MISSION_HK_STALE_RPT_TLM_TOPICID` (default 0xA2) and `HK_STALE_RPT_TLM_MID` (0x08A2 in this mission) |
+| `fsw/inc/hk_events.h` | `HK_STALE_CYCLES_INF_EID` 38, `HK_STALE_CYCLES_ERR_EID` 39, `HK_INPUT_STALE_EID` 40, `HK_INPUT_FRESH_EID` 41 |
+| `fsw/src/hk_app.[ch]` | `HK_AppData` holds `StaleCycles`, `StaleInputCount`, `StaleTransitionCtr`, per-entry `MissedCycles[]` and `InputStale[]`, and the report packet. `HK_AppInit` sets `StaleCycles = HK_STALE_CYCLES`; `HK_ResetHkData` (RESET_COUNTERS) zeroes `StaleTransitionCtr` only |
+| `fsw/src/hk_utils.[ch]` | New `HK_UpdateStaleness()`, called by `HK_SendCombinedHkPacket` once per combined send just before the data-present flags are cleared: present data resets the entry's missed cycles, missing data increments them (saturating at 0xFFFF), and staleness is re-evaluated against the current threshold with stale/fresh events. `HK_ProcessIncomingHkData` resets the missed cycles of each entry whose data it copies and sends the fresh event if that entry was stale. `HK_ProcessNewCopyTable` (startup and every table load) clears all missed cycles and stale states without events |
+| `fsw/src/hk_cmds.[ch]` | `HK_SendHkCmd` copies the three new fields; new `HK_SetStaleCyclesCmd` and `HK_ReportStaleCmd` |
+| `fsw/src/hk_dispatch.c` | Dispatch with HK's existing length check (`HK_VerifyCmdLength`, error counter on bad length) |
+| `fsw/tables/hk_cpy_tbl.c` | Entry 5: `SAMPLE_APP_HK_TLM_MID` offset 12 -> `HK_COMBINED_PKT2_MID` offset 12, 2 bytes |
+| `docs/dox_src/cfs_hk.dox` | User's guide section "Monitoring input staleness" |
+
+Event texts (MIDs as `0x` + 8 hex digits, as in HK's other events):
+
+* 38: `Stale cycles threshold set to %u`
+* 39: `Invalid stale cycles threshold %u, must be 1 to 255`
+* 40: `Input 0x%08lX for output 0x%08lX is stale, %u combined sends without data`
+* 41: `Input 0x%08lX for output 0x%08lX is fresh`
+
+### Mission configuration
+
+* `sample_defs/tables/to_lab_sub.c`: `HK_STALE_RPT_TLM_MID` forwarded to the ground.
+* `sample_defs/cpu1|cpu2/install_custom.cmake`: the HK table build gets SAMPLE_APP's include
+  directories (the same mechanism the file already uses for the TO_LAB and SCH_LAB tables);
+  without it `hk_cpy_tbl.c` cannot include `sample_app_msgids.h`.
+
+### Unit tests (`apps/hk/unit-test`)
+
+* `hk_utils_tests.c`: `HK_UpdateStaleness` becoming stale exactly at the threshold with one
+  event and no repeat, threshold raised (fresh event at the next send), threshold lowered (stale
+  event), only entries of the sent packet with an output buffer are touched, saturation, threshold
+  0; fresh on arrival in `HK_ProcessIncomingHkData`, a too-short input packet leaves the entry
+  stale; table reload clears all staleness without events; an end-to-end sequence through
+  `HK_SendCombinedHkPacket` and `HK_ProcessIncomingHkData` with exact event counts and order.
+* `hk_cmds_tests.c`: new housekeeping fields; SET_STALE_CYCLES with 1, 255 and 0 (counters,
+  event ID/type/text); REPORT_STALE with none, some (copy-table order, invalid unused slots) and
+  more than 16 stale entries.
+* `hk_dispatch_tests.c`: both new command codes with good and bad length.
+* `hk_app_tests.c`: `HK_AppInit` sets the default threshold; `HK_ResetHkData` zeroes
+  `StaleTransitionCtr` and keeps the stale states and the threshold.
+* Stubs for `HK_UpdateStaleness`, `HK_SetStaleCyclesCmd`, `HK_ReportStaleCmd`.
+  `HK_Test_Setup` now sets `HK_AppData.StaleCycles = HK_STALE_CYCLES` after the memset (the app's
+  real start-up value), and the event-capture depth was raised from 5 to 16.
+
+### CTF
+
+* `ctf/ccdd/json/hk_cmd.json`: `HK_SET_STALE_CYCLES_CC`, `HK_REPORT_STALE_CC`.
+* `ctf/ccdd/json/hk_hk_tlm.json`: the four appended housekeeping fields.
+* `ctf/ccdd/json/hk_stale_report_tlm.json` (new): `HK_STALE_RPT_TLM_MID` / `HK_StaleReportTlm_t`.
+* `ctf/ccdd/json/mission_mids.json`: `HK_STALE_RPT_TLM_MID` = 0x08A2;
+  `mission_constants.json`: `#HK_COMBINED_PKT2_MID#` = 0x089D for the request payload.
+* `ctf/ccdd/tools/layout_probe.c`: MIDs, command codes, sizes and offsets of the new items.
+  Probe output: `HK_HkPacket_t` 36 bytes (new fields at 28/30/32/33), `HK_SetStaleCyclesCmd_t`
+  12 bytes (`StaleCycles` at 8), `HK_ReportStaleCmd_t` 8, `HK_StaleReportTlm_t` 148 bytes
+  (`StaleCount` 16, `ReportedCount` 18, `InputMid` 20, `OutputMid` 84). No compiler padding;
+  the JSON matches these offsets (`check_layout.py`, mentioned in `ccdd/README.md`, is not in
+  the tree, so the comparison was done by reading the probe output).
+* `ctf/tests/hk_staleness.json` (new), tests:
+  1. `STALE-BOOT`: register, start, enable TO_LAB output.
+  2. `STALE-THRESHOLD`: RESET_COUNTERS; housekeeping shows `StaleCycles` 3; SET_STALE_CYCLES 0
+     gives event 39; SET_STALE_CYCLES 2 gives event 38; housekeeping shows 2, command counter 1,
+     error counter 1.
+  3. `STALE-STALE`: wait for a SAMPLE_APP housekeeping packet, request combined packet 2 three
+     times back to back, then check housekeeping `StaleInputCount` 1 and `StaleTransitionCtr` 1,
+     the report (one entry, 0x0883 -> 0x089D, next slot 0), and event 40 naming both MIDs.
+  4. `STALE-FRESH`: wait for the next SAMPLE_APP housekeeping packet, request combined packet 2,
+     check event 41, `StaleInputCount` 0, `StaleTransitionCtr` still 1, empty report.
+  5. `STALE-RESET`: RESET_COUNTERS zeroes `StaleTransitionCtr`, threshold stays 2.
+  6. `STALE-SHUTDOWN`.
+
+  Commanded telemetry is requested and checked with `wait: 0`. With a pre-instruction wait, CTF
+  discards the response to SEND_HK / REPORT_STALE as older than the verification start, then
+  the check waits for the next scheduled housekeeping packet, by which time SAMPLE_APP data may
+  already have made the entry fresh. The first draft of the test failed this way.
+
+## Unit test counts
+
+`make native_std.prep && make -j native_std.install && make -j native_std.runtest` on a clean
+`build-native_std`: build has no warnings (`-Werror`), all 191 test runners pass (same number of
+runners as before; HK still has four).
