+HK 38: Stale cycles threshold set to 2
+HK 40: Input 0x00000883 for output 0x0000089D is stale, 2 combined sends without data
+HK 41: Input 0x00000883 for output 0x0000089D is fresh
+```
+
+The same scenario was also driven without CTF, through `tools/run_cfs.sh` and
+`tools/udp_harness.py` (raw UDP, decoding events, HK housekeeping and the report packet). All
+checks passed: default threshold 3; events 39 and 38; exactly one stale event naming both MIDs;
+no repeat on a fourth send; housekeeping 1/1/2; report `StaleCount` 1, `ReportedCount` 1,
+`InputMid[0]` 0x883, `OutputMid[0]` 0x89D, other slots 0; exactly one fresh event; housekeeping
+0/1/2 and an empty report; RESET_COUNTERS gives `StaleTransitionCtr` 0 with the threshold still 2.
+Payload lengths on the wire: housekeeping 20 bytes, report 132 bytes.
+
+## Design decisions and assumptions
+
+* Per-entry state lives in `HK_AppData`, not in the dump-only runtime table, so the runtime
+  table's layout (and its EDS definition) is unchanged.
+* "Arrival" means the entry's data was actually copied. An input packet too short for the entry
+  (the existing `HK_ACCESSING_PAST_PACKET_END_EID` case) does not reset missed cycles or make the
+  entry fresh, which matches the data-present flag.
+* Entries sharing one input MID are tracked separately; one arriving packet can make several of
+  them fresh, with one event each.
+* A threshold of 0 cannot be commanded or configured. If `StaleCycles` were ever 0 (for example
+  in a unit-test fixture that zeroes `HK_AppData`), staleness detection is treated as disabled
+  instead of every entry being stale on its first miss.
+* Missed cycles are counted for every combined send, including sends that
+  `HK_DISCARD_INCOMPLETE_COMBO` suppresses.
+* On a combined send the order of events is: the existing missing-data debug event, then stale or
+  fresh events in copy-table order.
+* The report packet is built in `HK_AppData` and re-initialised by every REPORT_STALE command.
+* The new table and the TO_LAB subscription are configured for both cpu1 and cpu2 (both build
+  the same app list).
+
+## Open issues
+
+* EDS builds are not updated. `eds/hk.xml` and `hk_eds_dispatch.c` do not describe the two new
+  commands, the report packet or the extended housekeeping payload. The native_std (non-EDS)
+  configuration used here does not compile them.
+* `ctf/ccdd/tools/check_layout.py`, referenced by `ctf/ccdd/README.md`, is missing from the
+  tree. The layout was checked by hand against `probe_layout.sh` output.
+* `apps/hk/docs/hk_FunctionalRequirements.csv` has no requirements for the new behaviour yet.
+* In this sandbox `tools/stop_cfs.sh` reports "would not stop" after cFS exits: the process is
+  left defunct (not reaped by the parent shell), so `kill -0` still succeeds. Nothing keeps
+  listening on the UDP ports. This is an environment issue, not something the HK change causes.
